# The same family, and older than the repair (the skeptic seat's `y_r4`): a
# remark after a group's last member, then a doc directly above a second head
# with the same header and a blank line under it. Merged, the remark and the
# doc are printed at the members' column, one run the re-parse would read as
# the doc of both, so the remark takes the blank line that keeps it a remark
# and the doc gains none. The trunk refused it at exit 2, and the first repair
# too; the same with the remark at column 2 is the shape beside it.

extern "x.h"
    record Ob tag ob
    # a remark about Ob, at the members' column
# the doc of Pool
extern "x.h"

    record Pool tag pool
  # a remark about Pool, at column 2
# the doc of pool_new
extern "x.h"

    function pool_new() -> Pool

function main()
    print(0)
